IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vocfa-core`
IMPORT `vocfa-seat`

-- Cases for the applicant's seat (vocfa-seat.l4) and the regulative rules of the core (vocfa-core.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited Act (A2016-12 R10) and Regulation (SL2016-10 R11), never
-- copied from the encoding's output; the arithmetic is in the comment above each assertion.
-- No scenario life raised this Act: the people are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout, all in the ACT.
--
-- The eleven victim answers, in order: the day of the act; the offence; the person harmed is a partner or relative of
-- the offender; what the application is about; the harm; the harm came directly from the act; whether anyone died; the
-- relationship to the person who died; dependent on them; present at the homicide or a witness; took part in it.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the
-- trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. Clock: days.

-- Shorthand for the answers used below.
`assault`                 MEANS `an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2`
`sexual assault`          MEANS `a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3`
`image abuse`             MEANS `intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A`
`family violence offence` MEANS `an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)`
`own injury`              MEANS `an injury to the applicant`
`a death`                 MEANS `the death of a person killed by the act`
`injured`                 MEANS `a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one`
`violation only`          MEANS `only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity`
`nobody died`             MEANS `no one died as a result of the act`
`murdered`                MEANS `a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death`
`killed otherwise`        MEANS `a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence`
`no relation`             MEANS `another relationship, or none`
`all payments`            MEANS LIST `an immediate need payment (s 26)`, `an economic loss payment (s 27)`, `a recognition payment (ss 28 to 30)`
`no recognition`          MEANS LIST `an immediate need payment (s 26)`, `an economic loss payment (s 27)`
`s 98 not covered`        MEANS `an act of violence before 1 July 2016: applications for criminal injuries before the Act (s 98) are not encoded`
`ACAT not covered`        MEANS `review by the ACAT (part 9, s 95): its procedure and time limit are in the ACT Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2008, which is not deposited`

`1 Dec 2015`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2015
`5 Feb 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 2 2026
`14 Mar 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 14 3 2026
`10 Jun 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 6 2026
`1 Aug 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2026
`1 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2026
`15 Sep 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 9 2026
`20 Nov 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2026
`29 Feb 2028` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028
`2 May 1991`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 5 1991
`7 Jul 1995`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 7 7 1995
`1 Feb 2010`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2010
`3 Mar 2016`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2016

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. A primary victim. HYPOTHETICAL: Mia, born 2 May 1991, is beaten by a stranger in Civic on 14 March 2026 and
-- suffers grievous bodily harm. Offence against the person (Crimes Act pt 2).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 11: injured as a direct result of an act of violence (s 7: injury, sch 1 div 1.2.1 item 1, after 1 July 2016).
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a primary victim (s 11)`
-- s 19: all three payments.
#ASSERT `Which payments can I apply for` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may apply for` `all payments`
-- s 24, reg s 5 (1) (a): $67 959.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can receive for one application` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 67959

-- Immediate need (table 6). Security $4 500 (item 2 cap $4 000) + relocation $3 000 (item 3 cap $4 000) = $7 000; the
-- $2 000 emergency medical costs (item 4) are not available because Mia can afford them.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for an immediate need` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4500 3000 2000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 7000
-- If she cannot afford them: 4 000 + 3 000 + 2 000 = 9 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for an immediate need` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4500 3000 2000 TRUE 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 9000
-- Emergency medical $8 000: 4 000 + 3 000 + 8 000 = 15 000, over the reg s 6 (4) aggregate of $10 000 for the act.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for an immediate need` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4500 3000 8000 TRUE 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 10000

-- Economic loss (table 7), kind by kind. Lost earnings $42 000: item 6 cap $30 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for this economic loss` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `loss of actual earnings` 42000 FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 30000
-- Justice related $6 200: item 5 cap $5 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for this economic loss` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `justice related expenses` 6200 FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 5000
-- A phone and clothes worth $2 000: item 9 cap $1 500 (primary victim only).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for this economic loss` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `loss of or damage to personal items` 2000 FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 1500
-- Medical $12 000: item 3 has no cap.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for this economic loss` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `medical and dental expenses` 12000 FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 12000
-- Counselling $1 800: item 1 only if appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for this economic loss` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `expenses for counselling or other psychological support` 1800 FALSE EQUALS `none: not available for this loss or need to this applicant (reg ss 6 and 7, column 3)`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for this economic loss` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `expenses for counselling or other psychological support` 1800 TRUE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 1800

-- Recognition (table 8): item 4, offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm, $10 873.
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 10873
-- Item 1 ("sexual offence") does not fit an offence against the person.
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more` FALSE EQUALS `none: the act of violence did not occur in the course of an offence in table 8 (reg s 8)`
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the offences in table 8` FALSE EQUALS `none: the act of violence did not occur in the course of an offence in table 8 (reg s 8)`

-- All claims together. Immediate need 4 000 + 3 000 + 2 000 = 9 000. Economic loss: applying 200, medical 12 000,
-- travel 800, justice 6 200 -> 5 000, earnings 42 000 -> 30 000, items 2 000 -> 1 500: 49 500. Recognition 10 873.
-- 9 000 + 49 500 + 10 873 = 69 373, over the $67 959 maximum: 67 959.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be given on my application, all claims together` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4500 3000 2000 TRUE 0 0 200 12000 800 6200 42000 0 0 2000 FALSE TRUE `an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 67959
-- With $2 500 of insurance for the same loss (s 47 (2) (a)), reduced after the maximum: 67 959 - 2 500 = 65 459.
-- (Reduced before the maximum it would be 69 373 - 2 500 = 66 873: see NOTES.md.)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be given on my application, all claims together` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4500 3000 2000 TRUE 0 0 200 12000 800 6200 42000 0 0 2000 FALSE TRUE `an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2500 0 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 65459
-- Without the recognition claim: 9 000 + 49 500 = 58 500, under the maximum; less 2 500 = 56 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be given on my application, all claims together` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4500 3000 2000 TRUE 0 0 200 12000 800 6200 42000 0 0 2000 FALSE FALSE `an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2500 0 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 56000
-- s 45 (1) (e): if the commissioner finds she unreasonably failed to help the police, nothing may be given.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be given on my application, all claims together` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4500 3000 2000 TRUE 0 0 200 12000 800 6200 42000 0 0 2000 FALSE TRUE `an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 EQUALS `none: financial assistance must not be given, as a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45)`

-- s 45 alone.
#ASSERT `Must financial assistance be refused to me` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no disqualifying circumstance applies on these findings (s 45)`
#ASSERT `Must financial assistance be refused to me` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `assistance must not be given: a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45 (1) (b) to (e), (4))`
-- (d) is for a related victim: a finding about the primary victim's own serious crime does not disqualify Mia under (d).
#ASSERT `Must financial assistance be refused to me` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no disqualifying circumstance applies on these findings (s 45)`
-- s 47: 2 500 associated + 1 000 unpaid repayment + 500 for contributory conduct = 4 000.
#ASSERT `By how much must my assistance be reduced` 2500 1000 500 EQUALS 4000

-- s 31. Mia is 34, the offence is not a sexual offence, and no other s 31 (4) ground: a police report is needed.
#ASSERT `What evidence of reporting must my application include` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 May 1991` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `evidence that the act was reported to a police officer (s 31 (2) (d) (i))`
#ASSERT `Does my application meet the requirements of s 31` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 May 1991` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- No police report, only a government agency and a doctor: not enough for someone outside the special reporting class.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application meet the requirements of s 31` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 May 1991` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Not in writing: fails s 31 (2) (a).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application meet the requirements of s 31` `14 Mar 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 May 1991` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 32 (1): 3 years from 14 March 2026 (her 18th birthday, 2 May 2009, is earlier): 14 March 2029.
#ASSERT `What is the last day to apply for financial assistance` `14 Mar 2026` `2 May 1991` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 14 3 2029
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `14 Mar 2026` `2 May 1991` (DATE_FROM_DMY 14 3 2029) EQUALS `in time: made on or before the last day (s 32 (1))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `14 Mar 2026` `2 May 1991` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2029) EQUALS `late: the commissioner may extend the time if satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is in the interests of fairness, having regard to the person's age at the act, impaired capacity, a person responsible in a position of power, trust or authority, the effect of the act, and whether a fair consideration is still possible (s 32 (2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. A special reporting class victim. HYPOTHETICAL: Ella, born 1 February 2010, is sexually assaulted by her
-- sports coach on 5 February 2026, aged 16. Sexual offence (Crimes Act pt 3), punishable by 10 to 14 years.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a primary victim (s 11)`
-- s 9 (1) (c): a sense of violation alone is an injury when it comes from a sexual offence.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `violation only` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a primary victim (s 11)`

-- s 31 (4): a primary victim of a sexual offence (and under 18, and the coach in a position of trust).
-- Immediate need only: s 31 (5) (a), at least 2 of the 3 bodies.
#ASSERT `What evidence of reporting must my application include` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2010` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `evidence of a police report, or of reports to at least 2 of: a government agency; a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker; an appropriately qualified non-government agency (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (a))`
-- Economic loss only, or with immediate need: s 31 (5) (b), both a government agency and a practitioner.
#ASSERT `What evidence of reporting must my application include` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `evidence of a police report, or of reports to both a government agency and a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (b))`
#ASSERT `What evidence of reporting must my application include` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2010` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `evidence of a police report, or of reports to both a government agency and a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (b))`
-- With a recognition payment claimed, s 31 (2) (d) (ii) is closed: a police report is needed.
#ASSERT `What evidence of reporting must my application include` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2010` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `evidence that the act was reported to a police officer (s 31 (2) (d) (i))`
-- Economic loss only, reported to the Directorate and a counsellor, not to police: meets s 31 (2).
#ASSERT `Does my application meet the requirements of s 31` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Immediate need only, reported to a counsellor and a listed non-government agency: 2 of 3, meets it.
#ASSERT `Does my application meet the requirements of s 31` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2010` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Immediate need only, reported to a counsellor alone: 1 of 3, does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application meet the requirements of s 31` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2010` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Economic loss and recognition, reported to the Directorate and a counsellor but not to police: does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application meet the requirements of s 31` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Table 8 item 3: $10 873; under reg s 8 (3), where Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies, item 6: $2 716.
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years` FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 10873
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years` TRUE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 2716
-- Item 1, 14 years or more: $20 386.
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `5 Feb 2026` `sexual assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more` FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 20386

-- s 32 (1) (c): she was 16, so the 3 years run from her 18th birthday, 1 February 2028: last day 1 February 2031.
#ASSERT `What is the last day to apply for financial assistance` `5 Feb 2026` `1 Feb 2010` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2031
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `5 Feb 2026` `1 Feb 2010` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2031) EQUALS `in time: made on or before the last day (s 32 (1))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `5 Feb 2026` `1 Feb 2010` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 2 2031) EQUALS `late: the commissioner may extend the time if satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is in the interests of fairness, having regard to the person's age at the act, impaired capacity, a person responsible in a position of power, trust or authority, the effect of the act, and whether a fair consideration is still possible (s 32 (2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. Intimate image abuse. HYPOTHETICAL: Noah, born 7 July 1995, finds on 10 June 2026 that a stranger has shared
-- intimate images of him (Crimes Act pt 3A).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A sense of violation alone: not an injury, since intimate image abuse is not a "sexual offence" (dictionary: items 2,
-- 4 and 5 only) and a stranger is not a relevant person. No injury, no death: no act of violence (s 7 (1) (a)).
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `10 Jun 2026` `image abuse` FALSE `own injury` `violation only` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a victim: the conduct is not an act of violence (s 7)`
-- With a diagnosed depressive illness (a mental illness): a primary victim.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `10 Jun 2026` `image abuse` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a primary victim (s 11)`
-- Shared by his former partner (a relevant person): a family violence offence (s 9 (2)), so the s 9 (1) (c) harm counts.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `10 Jun 2026` `image abuse` TRUE `own injury` `violation only` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a primary victim (s 11)`
-- Not a sexual offence, adult, no other s 31 (4) ground: not a special reporting class victim, so a police report.
#ASSERT `What evidence of reporting must my application include` `10 Jun 2026` `image abuse` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `7 Jul 1995` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `evidence that the act was reported to a police officer (s 31 (2) (d) (i))`
-- Table 8's sexual offence items do not reach intimate image abuse.
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `10 Jun 2026` `image abuse` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years` FALSE EQUALS `none: the act of violence did not occur in the course of an offence in table 8 (reg s 8)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 4. A division 1.2.2 family violence offence. HYPOTHETICAL: Priya's former partner smashes her car and front door
-- on 1 September 2026 (Crimes Act s 116); she develops an anxiety disorder.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `1 Sep 2026` `family violence offence` TRUE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a primary victim (s 11)`
-- The same damage by a stranger is not a schedule 1 offence (dictionary, "schedule 1 offence" (b)).
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `1 Sep 2026` `family violence offence` FALSE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a victim: the conduct is not an act of violence (s 7)`
-- Reg s 5 (2): an application only about a division 1.2.2 offence: $13 590, not $67 959.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can receive for one application` `1 Sep 2026` `family violence offence` TRUE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 13590
-- Security 4 000 + relocation 4 000 = 8 000 immediate need; lost earnings 8 000; 16 000 in all, capped at 13 590.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be given on my application, all claims together` `1 Sep 2026` `family violence offence` TRUE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4000 4000 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 8000 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none of the offences in table 8` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 13590
-- Table 8's offence-against-the-person items do not reach a division 1.2.2 offence.
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `1 Sep 2026` `family violence offence` TRUE `own injury` `injured` TRUE `nobody died` `no relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm` FALSE EQUALS `none: the act of violence did not occur in the course of an offence in table 8 (reg s 8)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 5. A homicide. HYPOTHETICAL: Daniel is murdered by a stranger on 1 August 2026. His domestic partner Sarah
-- depended on him; his son Liam (25) and sister Grace did not; his brother Tom (15) did, but Daniel was not his
-- guardian; his grandmother; Jess, a passer-by who saw it and developed post-traumatic stress disorder.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 13: Sarah, domestic partner (close family member, s 17 (1) (a)) and a dependant: class A.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a class A related victim (s 13)`
#ASSERT `Which payments can I apply for` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may apply for` `all payments`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can receive for one application` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 40773
-- Reg s 9: $27 183, whatever the offence.
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the offences in table 8` FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 27183
-- Cleaning the scene, $6 000: item 1 cap $5 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for an immediate need` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE 6000 0 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 5000
-- Reg s 6 (4) counts every immediate need payment for the act: $7 000 already paid to Daniel's mother leaves $3 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be paid for an immediate need` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE 6000 0 0 0 FALSE 7000 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 3000
-- Cleaning 5 000 + earnings 35 000 -> 30 000 + recognition 27 183 = 62 183, capped at 40 773.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be given on my application, all claims together` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE 6000 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 35000 0 0 0 FALSE TRUE `none of the offences in table 8` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 40773
-- s 45 (1) (d): a related victim, where the act was related to a serious crime by Daniel: nothing may be given.
#ASSERT `Must financial assistance be refused to me` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `assistance must not be given: a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45 (1) (b) to (e), (4))`
-- s 16: Sarah, who also saw it, is a related victim, so cannot be a homicide witness for her own shock.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `own injury` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `the domestic partner` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not a victim in that capacity (ss 11 to 16)`

-- s 14: Liam, his son, financially independent: class B; reg s 5 (1) (c) $27 183; reg s 10 $13 590.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim, and of which class` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a class B related victim (s 14)`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can receive for one application` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 27183
#ASSERT `What recognition payment can I get` `1 Aug 2026` `assault` FALSE `a death` `injured` FALSE `murdered` `a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian` FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the offences in table 8` FALSE EQUALS `the most that can be paid, in dollars` 13590
-- An intimate partner who was not a domestic partner, financially independent: class B too.
